a shape is one of:
    a circle with a radius (a number).
    a square with a side (a number).
let shapes be a list of (a new circle with radius 20), (a new circle with radius 2) and (a new square with side 3).
for each s in shapes:
    check which kind s is:
        when it's a circle whose radius is over 10:
            say "big circle", its radius.
        when it's a circle:
            say "small circle".
        when it's a square where its side is 3:
            say "square of 3".
        otherwise:
            say "other square".
